<quiz>
<question type="stack">
  <name><text>Area of an image from the determinant</text></name>
  <questiontext format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>The [[if test="is(sh=\"rect\")"]]rectangle with vertices \(({@V1[1]@},\,{@V1[2]@})\), \(({@V2[1]@},\,{@V2[2]@})\), \(({@V3[1]@},\,{@V3[2]@})\) and \(({@V4[1]@},\,{@V4[2]@})\)[[else]]right-angled triangle with vertices \(({@V1[1]@},\,{@V1[2]@})\), \(({@V2[1]@},\,{@V2[2]@})\) and \(({@V4[1]@},\,{@V4[2]@})\)[[/if]] is mapped by \(M = {@Mt@}\).</p><p>(a) Find \(\det M\).</p><div>[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]] [[feedback:prt1]]</div><p>(b) Find the area of the image.</p><div>[[input:ans2]] square units [[validation:ans2]] [[feedback:prt2]]</div><p>(c) The orientation of the image is</p><div>[[input:ans3]] [[validation:ans3]] [[feedback:prt3]]</div>]]></text>
  </questiontext>
  <generalfeedback format="html">
    <text><![CDATA[<p>(a) \(\det M = ad - bc = {@dm@}\).</p><p>(b) The [[if test="is(sh=\"rect\")"]]rectangle is \({@w@}\) by \({@h@}\), so its area is \({@ar@}\)[[else]]triangle has base \({@w@}\) and height \({@h@}\), so its area is \({@ar@}\)[[/if]]. The area scale factor is \(|\det M| = {@abs(dm)@}\), so the area of the image is \({@abs(dm)@} \times {@ar@} = {@ta2@}\) square units.</p><p>(c) The determinant tells you how many times bigger every area becomes, and its sign tells you whether the shape has been turned over. [[if test="is(dm<0)"]]Here \(\det M \lt 0\), so the orientation is reversed.[[else]]Here \(\det M > 0\), so the orientation is the same.[[/if]]</p>]]></text>
  </generalfeedback>
  <defaultgrade>3</defaultgrade>
  <penalty>0.1</penalty>
  <hidden>0</hidden>
  <idnumber></idnumber>
  <stackversion><text>2026063000</text></stackversion>
  <questionvariables>
    <text><![CDATA[/* Design: determinant as area scale factor; a negative sign reverses orientation. Source: adapted from SMP Book 5 (Metric), Chapter 14, Section 4.2. 5 negative and 5 positive determinants; ad + bc, bc - ad, area / |det|, det^2 x area and the follow-through value differ from the answers on every entry. */
alist: [[matrix([1,3],[5,5]),"rect",3,4,0,-2],[matrix([3,-4],[-4,2]),"tri",2,3,2,1],[matrix([3,3],[2,5]),"rect",4,2,2,-1],[matrix([-4,-2],[1,1]),"tri",3,3,0,1],[matrix([5,-4],[-2,2]),"tri",2,4,-1,2],[matrix([5,2],[2,-1]),"tri",5,4,-2,-1],[matrix([2,5],[-1,1]),"rect",4,2,-1,0],[matrix([-3,-1],[4,3]),"tri",5,4,-2,-1],[matrix([-2,-1],[-1,2]),"rect",4,4,2,2],[matrix([2,-2],[1,5]),"tri",3,3,-2,0]];
ix: 1+rand(10);
Mt: alist[ix][1]; sh: alist[ix][2]; w: alist[ix][3]; h: alist[ix][4]; x0: alist[ix][5]; y0: alist[ix][6];
V1: [x0,y0]; V2: [x0+w,y0]; V3: [x0+w,y0+h]; V4: [x0,y0+h];
ar: if sh="rect" then w*h else w*h/2;
dm: determinant(Mt);
ta2: abs(dm)*ar;
orn: if dm<0 then "rev" else "same";
oth: if dm<0 then "same" else "rev";
opt3: [["imp",false,"impossible to tell from M"],["same",is(orn="same"),"the same as the object's"],["rev",is(orn="rev"),"reversed"]];
/* diagnostics: (a) ad + bc, bc - ad; (b) area / |det|, det^2 x area */
dSum: Mt[1,1]*Mt[2,2]+Mt[1,2]*Mt[2,1]; dRev: -dm;
dDiv: ar/abs(dm); dSq: dm^2*ar;
ftS: abs(dSum)*ar;
tw1: dm+1; tw2: ta2+1;
]]></text>
  </questionvariables>
