  <questiondescription format="html"><text><![CDATA[<p id="concept">Matrices and Transformations: area of an image from the determinant</p><p id="description">Grade 12 CBE Core 2.1: Find the determinant of a matrix, the area of the image of a rectangle or triangle, and whether the orientation is reversed.</p><p id="edition">Core</p><p id="provenance">This question is adapted from Chapter 14, Section 4.2 of School Mathematics Project, SMP Book 5 (Metric), ed. P. G. Bowie, Cambridge University Press, 1969: applied to a given rectangle or triangle with the orientation asked for, new matrices and shapes, randomised, with named and follow-through feedback.</p><p id="citation">INNODEMS CBC Grade 12 Mathematics, first draft by Ben Davies, 2026. Aligned to the KICD Senior School Curriculum Design, Core Mathematics Grade 12 (draft).</p>]]></text></questiondescription>
